From: Pat Wendorf <dungeons@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] battery: no keyboard backlight slider without a keyboard backlight

UPower (1.91.5) exports /org/freedesktop/UPower/KbdBacklight on every
machine and answers GetMaxBrightness = 0 when there is no keyboard
backlight LED. The applet took any answer as a backlight, so every
desktop and most laptops showed a keyboard slider reading "NaN%"
(100 * 0 / 0), and a machine with no adjustable screen either would
have shown a keyboard icon in the panel. Treat a maximum of 0 as no
backlight and ignore brightness updates until a real maximum arrives.

Upstream: unfixed on master as of 2026-11-26
---
--- a/cosmic-applet-battery/src/app.rs
+++ b/cosmic-applet-battery/src/app.rs
@@ -431,10 +431,18 @@
                     self.kbd_sender = Some(tx);
                 }
                 KeyboardBacklightUpdate::MaxBrightness(max_brightness) => {
-                    self.max_kbd_brightness = Some(max_brightness);
+                    // UPower exports its KbdBacklight object on every machine and
+                    // answers 0 when there is no keyboard backlight. Treat that as
+                    // none: no slider (it read "NaN%", 0/0) and no keyboard icon.
+                    if max_brightness > 0 {
+                        self.max_kbd_brightness = Some(max_brightness);
+                    } else {
+                        self.max_kbd_brightness = None;
+                        self.kbd_brightness = None;
+                    }
                 }
                 KeyboardBacklightUpdate::Brightness(brightness) => {
-                    if !self.dragging_kbd_brightness {
+                    if !self.dragging_kbd_brightness && self.max_kbd_brightness.is_some() {
                         self.kbd_brightness = Some(brightness);
                     }
                 }
